MK</given-names></name><name><surname>Anderson</surname><given-names>DC</given-names></name><name><surname>Payan</surname><given-names>DG</given-names></name><name><surname>Lorens</surname><given-names>JB</given-names></name><name><surname>Bogenberger</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Demo</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Cellular localization and antiproliferative effect of peptides discovered from a functional screen of a retrovirally delivered random peptide library</article-title><source>Chem Biol</source><year>2003</year><volume>10</volume><fpage>975</fpage><lpage>987</lpage><!--PubMed citation query: 'Chem Biol||10|975||bib8|'--><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">14583264</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib9"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Honda</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Tanaka</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Yasuda</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Oncoprotein MDM2 is a ubiquitin ligase E3 for tumor suppressor p53</article-title><source>FEBS Lett</source><year>1997</year><volume>420</volume><fpage>25</fpage><lpage>27</lpage><!--PubMed citation query: 'FEBS Lett||420|25||bib9|'--><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9450543</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib10"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Hupp</surname><given-names>TR</given-names></name><name><surname>Sparks</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Lane</surname><given-names>DP</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Small peptides activate the latent sequence-specific DNA binding function of p53</article-title><source>Cell</source><year>1995</year><volume>83</volume><fpage>237</fpage><lpage>245</lpage><!--PubMed citation query: 'Cell||83|237||bib10|'--><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">7585941</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib11"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Ladner</surname><given-names>RC</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Constrained peptides as binding entities</article-title><source>Trends Biotechnol</source><year>1995</year><volume>13</volume><fpage>426</fpage><lpage>430</lpage><!--PubMed citation query: 'Trends Biotechnol||13|426||bib11|'--><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">7546567</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib12"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Mavilio</surname><given-names>F</given-names></name><name><surname>Ferrari</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>Rossini</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Nobili</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name><name><surname>Bonini</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Casorati</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>Traversari</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Bordignon</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Peripheral blood lymphocytes as target cells of retroviral vector-mediated gene transfer</article-title><source>Blood</source><year>1994</year><volume>83</volume><fpage>1988</fpage><lpage>1997</lpage><!--PubMed citation query: 'Blood||83|1988||bib12|'--><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8142665</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib13"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>McPhalen</surname><given-names>CA</given-names></name><name><surname>James</surname><given-names>MN</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Crystal and molecular structure of the serine proteinase inhibitor CI-2 from barley seeds</article-title><source>Biochemistry</source><year>1987</year><volume>26</volume><fpage>261</fpage><lpage>269</lpage><!--PubMed citation query: 'Biochemistry||26|261||bib13|'--><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">3828302</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib14"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Nolan</surname><given-names>GP</given-names></name><name><surname>Fiering</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Nicolas</surname><given-names>JF</given-names></name><name><surname>Herzenberg</surname><given-names>LA</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Fluorescence-activated cell analysis and sorting of viable mammalian cells based on beta-<sc>D</sc>-galactosidase activity after transduction of <italic>Escherichia coli</italic> lacZ</article-title><source>Proc Natl Acad Sci USA</source><year>1988</year><volume>85</volume><fpage>2603</fpage><lpage>2607</lpage><!--PubMed citation query: 'Proc Natl Acad Sci USA||85|2603||bib14|'--></citation></ref><ref id="bib15"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Nygren</surname><given-names>PA</given-names></name><name><surname>Uhlen</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Scaffolds for engineering novel binding sites in proteins</article-title><source>Curr Opin Struct Biol</source><year>1997</year><volume>7</volume><fpage>463</fpage><lpage>469</lpage><!--PubMed citation query: 'Curr Opin Struct Biol||7|463||bib15|'--><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9266166</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib16"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Osmark</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Sorensen</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Poulsen</surname><given-names>FM</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Context dependence of protein secondary structure formation: the three-dimensional structure and stability of a hybrid between chymotrypsin inhibitor 2 and helix E from subtilisin Carlsberg</article-title><source>Biochemistry</source><year>1993</year><volume>32</volume><fpage>11007</fpage